<article class="env-exercise" id="0DCJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DCJ">Exercise <span data-tag="0DCJ">111.45.6</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0DCE" data-tag="0DCE">111.45.1</a> assume $n = 2$. Let $s_1, s_2, s_3 \in \Gamma (X, \mathcal{O}_ X(2))$ be three quadric equations. Consider the coherent sheaf </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{F} = \mathop{\mathrm{Coker}}\left(\mathcal{O}_ X(-2)^{\oplus 3} \xrightarrow {s_1, s_2, s_3} \mathcal{O}_ X\right)  \]
</div>
  <p> List the possible Hilbert polynomials of such $\mathcal{F}$. (Try to visualize intersections of quadrics in the projective plane.) </p>
</article>